SC64 command busy time for the test harness (hl64; on the series before it).

meeq/ares' SC64 (ares/n64/sc64, Christopher Bonhage) runs every command at once: CMD_BUSY is
never seen set. ARES_SC64_SECTOR_US=<us> (default 0: unchanged) keeps SD_READ / SD_WRITE
busy for sectors * <us> of emulated time after the data moved (it moves at once): a
Queue::SC64_Command event then clears CMD_BUSY and raises CMD_IRQ_PENDING when the command
asked for it (CMD_IRQ_REQUEST), as the immediate path does. So the cart's pacing of
background SD fills sees non-instant commands; timing fidelity is not a goal.

